## Problem

# b00t datums ARE a typed ontology:
# - `b00t.type` = node type (agent, role, mcp, skill, prd, okr, stack, ...)
# - `[[b00t.agent.inherits]]` = inheritance edges
# - `🔗参` link comments = cross-datum references
# - `b00t:map v1` tail-maps = fast-scannable metadata

# l3dg3rr already has:
# - `ontology-extractor` crate — extracts typed graph from Rust source
# - `rotel-visual` crate — isometric SVG + Mermaid visualization
# - `mdbook-rhai-mermaid` — Rhai DSL → diagram rendering (PRD-3 in progress)
# - `plantuml` MCP server — available for TOGAF/MBSE diagram output

# But datums are not wired to any of these. Governance and architecture are invisible.

## Finished State

# `b00t datums graph --format=mermaid` emits Mermaid flowchart of all datums:
# - Nodes: one per datum, labeled with `b00t.type` + `b00t.name`
# - Edges: `inherits`, `🔗参` links, `links_tasks`, `stack_requires`
# - Color coding by tier (sm0l=green, ch0nky=yellow, frontier=red)

# `b00t datums graph --format=plantuml` → pipes through `plantuml` MCP → SVG output.

# Optional: expose as l3dg3rr `OntologyNode`/`OntologyEdge` format so `rotel-visual`
# renders the full hive architecture as isometric SVG (same as l3dg3rr's bookkeeping graph).

## Technical Approach

# l3dg3rr's `ontology-extractor` already has:
# ```rust
# pub struct OntologyNode { id, label, node_type, properties }
# pub struct OntologyEdge { from, to, edge_type, label }
# ```

# Add new input adapter: `TomllmOntologyAdapter` that reads `.tomllm`/`.tomllmd` files
# and emits `OntologyNode` + `OntologyEdge` without touching visualization code.

# Node extraction:
# - `b00t.name` → `id`
# - `b00t.type` → `node_type`
# - `b00t.hint` → `label`
# - `b00t:map v1` tags → `properties.tags`

# Edge extraction:
# - `[[b00t.agent.inherits]]` → `inherits` edge
# - `# 🔗参 <path>` comments → `references` edge
# - `links_tasks = [N]` → `linked_task` edge to task node
# - `stack_requires = ["X"]` → `requires` edge

## Acceptance Criteria

# - [ ] `TomllmOntologyAdapter::extract(dir) -> Vec<(OntologyNode, Vec<OntologyEdge>)>` in l3dg3rr
# - [ ] `b00t datums graph --format=mermaid` outputs valid Mermaid flowchart (render test)
# - [ ] All 30+ existing `.tomllm` datums appear as nodes
# - [ ] At least 10 typed edges extracted from existing `🔗参` comments
# - [ ] `b00t datums graph --format=plantuml` pipes to plantuml MCP → PNG/SVG
# - [ ] Optional: `rotel-visual` accepts tomllm ontology as input source

## Sub-tasks

# | # | title | tier | file |
